{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"328\tFor each `unrecognized` event it routes by `producer.source` to that adapter's\n329\t`renormalizeUnrecognized`, which re-feeds the stored `raw.data` through the\n330\t*same* `convertLine` the live capture loop uses, with the same identity-\n331\tdetermining inputs recovered from the preserved event: `conversation.seq`,\n332\tthe session id (in `raw.data` for Claude Code, in `producer.session_id` for\n333\tCodex), and — for a Codex line with no timestamp of its own — `occurred_at` as\n334\tthe `baseTime` fallback (which is exactly the `sessionBaseTime` value a live\n335\tcapture would compute). The turn therefore gets the byte-identical id a live\n336\tcapture of the same line would, so a later live capture dedups against it\n337\tinstead of duplicating — the property the whole scheme rests on. When the\n338\tadapter still cannot interpret the line (`convertLine` returns null, e.g. a\n339\ttimestampless Claude line, or a genuinely unknown type) it stays preserved.\n340\t\n341\tThe rewrite is append-only and idempotent: the `unrecognized` event is never\n342\tdeleted but superseded by a `supersession` event carrying\n343\t`links:[{rel:\"supersedes\",target}]` (mirroring how `cledger redact` records a\n344\trewrite via a companion event). Re-runs are no-ops — already-superseded events\n345\tare skipped, and every produced id (turn and supersession) is deterministic,\n346\tso anything that slips through dedups on append. The reconstructed turn's\n347\t`raw.data` is the already-redacted stored copy and rides the normal\n348\t`appendEvents` redaction path, which is idempotent on placeholdered text, so\n349\tnothing is re-exposed and the recomputed id is stable. Encrypted/opaque\n350\t`reasoning` payloads can never reach this path (they are never preserved) and\n351\t`convertLine` refuses them regardless, so re-normalization never reconstructs\n352\tprovide